# Otto Simulator (`simulate.py`)

Python 3.10+; always `source .venv/bin/activate` first. Emulates full Otto hardware from `microcode.py` + kernel ROM.

## Headless / automated testing

```bash
python simulate.py --autorun --program roms/apps/asm/myapp.bin --max-cycles 1000000 --quiet
echo $?   # 0=success, 1=timeout, 2=error
```

| Flag | Effect |
|------|--------|
| `--autorun` | Headless; pre-sends `r`+CR to run program at load address |
| `--quiet` | Suppress kernel boot output; show app output only |
| `--max-cycles N` | Safety limit (0=unlimited) |
| `--address 0xADDR` | Load address (default 0x8400) |
| `--input '...'` | Scripted keyboard input |
| `--dump-regs FILE` | JSON register dump on exit |
| `--serial-device PATH` | Real serial port for ACIA (e.g. FTDI → VGA32) |
| `--serial-baud N` | Baud for `--serial-device` (default 115200) |

Programs ending with **`RTS`** or **`HLT`** exit cleanly in autorun mode.

## Interactive / dev

```bash
python simulate.py --program roms/apps/asm/myapp.bin   # hot-reloads on recompile
python simulate.py --simulate-serial                    # virtual serial port (minicom)
python simulate.py --serial-device /dev/cu.usbserial-XXX  # real port (VGA32 / FTDI)
```

## Simulator-only

- `DMP` (0xF7) dumps registers to console — no effect on real hardware
- `OUT` register can serve as halt return code

Memory regions and I/O details: `AGENTS.md`.
